          "created_at": "2026-08-13T05:08:17.223Z",
          "cooked": "<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/vlad_gerasimchuk\">@Vlad_Gerasimchuk</a> ,<br>\nThis is actually a really useful idea. CSV imports can be risky because the file can look perfectly fine in Excel while still causing unexpected changes once Shopify processes it.</p>\n<p>definitely add checks around variant data and image mapping too. Those are the kinds of issues that can be difficult to notice until after the import is complete, especially with larger catalogs.</p>\n<p>I like that the checker runs locally and doesn’t require uploading the store data anywhere. Thats a big plus for merchants who are dealing with sensitive product and supplier information.</p>",
