    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1733139,
      "summarized_text": "A free, browser-based Shopify CSV checker is intended to catch import problems that may silently remove variants or disrupt product data. Its creator says it flags missing option columns when SKU or Weight is present, Excel-damaged SKUs, inconsistent handles, prices with currency symbols, inaccessible image URLs, and encoding issues. The file stays on the user’s device, and the checker works offline after loading.\n\nReplies support pre-checking imports and suggest additional checks for image compatibility, expiring URL parameters, and variant-image assignments. Another commenter explains that Shopify may treat the rows for a product handle as its complete definition, so missing or malformed variant rows can result in lost variants without a warning. They recommend exporting a backup, comparing variant-row counts between the live catalog and import file, checking required option fields, and testing one product before a bulk import. One reply also promotes a separate local image-conversion tool. The discussion offers practical recommendations but does not report test results or establish whether the checker includes the suggested image checks.",
